sh: use xtrct again for the middle word of a 64-bit shift by 16

Since GCC 15, expand_subword_shift (optabs.cc) joins the two halves of a
DImode shift with PLUS instead of IOR.  The SH xtrct_left/xtrct_right
patterns only match the IOR form, so "(int32_t) (x >> 16)" on a 64-bit
value, the core of every 16.16 fixed point multiply
"(int32_t) (((int64_t) a * b) >> 16)", became shll16, shlr16 and add
(3 insns) instead of one xtrct.  The two halves do not share bits, so
PLUS and IOR give the same result: new patterns *xtrct_left_plus and
*xtrct_right_plus match the PLUS form too.

Measured on sh-elf -m2 (GDB SH simulator), GCC 16.2 with patch 0006,
without and with this patch:
- fx3d benchmark (16.16 fixed point 3D transform): 1,215,969 -> 1,134,049
  cycles at -O2 (-6.7%), 1,224,120 -> 1,142,200 at -Os (-6.7%), -5.4%
  at -O1; GCC 14.3: 1,138,145 and 1,142,192.
- GCC torture execute and compile suites, zlib and benchmarks at
  -O1/-O2/-O3/-Os: no compile failure, no change of any run result,
  only fx3d and two torture programs change (faster), .text 0.006% to
  0.012% smaller.
- Ported to 15.3.0: built and measured on 15.3.0 too, same results
  (fx3d -6.7% at -O2 and -Os, .text 0.008% smaller, no run result
  changes).
  Torture execute at -O1/-O2/-O3/-Os and compile at -O2/-Os with cc1
  15.3.0 built without and with this patch: no new compile failure, no run
  result change, 1 or 2 programs per level differ (-0.001% to -0.003%
  instructions).

--- a/gcc-15.3.0/gcc/config/sh/sh.md
+++ b/gcc-15.3.0/gcc/config/sh/sh.md
@@ -4383,6 +4383,29 @@
   "xtrct	%2,%0"
   [(set_attr "type" "arith")])
 
+;; Since GCC 15, expand_subword_shift combines the two halves of a DImode
+;; shift with PLUS instead of IOR.  The bits do not overlap, so PLUS is the
+;; same operation; match it too, else (int64) x >> 16 costs 3 insns.
+(define_insn "*xtrct_left_plus"
+  [(set (match_operand:SI 0 "arith_reg_dest" "=r")
+        (plus:SI (ashift:SI (match_operand:SI 1 "arith_reg_operand" "r")
+			    (const_int 16))
+		 (lshiftrt:SI (match_operand:SI 2 "arith_reg_operand" "0")
+			      (const_int 16))))]
+  "TARGET_SH1"
+  "xtrct	%1,%0"
+  [(set_attr "type" "arith")])
+
+(define_insn "*xtrct_right_plus"
+  [(set (match_operand:SI 0 "arith_reg_dest" "=r")
+        (plus:SI (lshiftrt:SI (match_operand:SI 1 "arith_reg_operand" "0")
+			      (const_int 16))
+		 (ashift:SI (match_operand:SI 2 "arith_reg_operand" "r")
+			    (const_int 16))))]
+  "TARGET_SH1"
+  "xtrct	%2,%0"
+  [(set_attr "type" "arith")])
+
 ;; -------------------------------------------------------------------------
 ;; Unary arithmetic
 ;; -------------------------------------------------------------------------
